WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.642
Hi, friends. Gani here. This is Big Feeling Detective.

00:00:12.642 --> 00:00:17.285
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:17.285 --> 00:00:20.070
Hands resting on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:22.856
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:31.212
Sometimes a feeling gets big before it has a name. It is just… big, and buzzy, and there.

00:00:31.212 --> 00:00:39.569
A detective does not guess right away. A detective looks for clues.

00:00:39.569 --> 00:00:45.140
Today we investigate one pretend big feeling, step by step, like detectives.

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:48.854
Every clue is welcome. There are no wrong clues.

00:00:48.854 --> 00:00:58.139
Step one: notice the body clues. Is the pretend face hot? Are the pretend hands tight, like fists?

00:00:58.139 --> 00:01:04.638
Are the pretend legs wiggly, wanting to move? Is the pretend tummy tight, or fluttery?

00:01:04.638 --> 00:01:12.995
Clues are not answers. Clues are hints — they point the way.

00:01:12.995 --> 00:01:22.280
Good detecting. We have our clues.

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:32.493
Step two: size it. Hold the feeling up against your body: is it small, medium, or big?

00:01:32.493 --> 00:01:38.064
Our pretend feeling feels big. That is fine — big is a size, not a problem.

00:01:38.064 --> 00:01:44.564
Step three: line up the suspect words. Might it be mad? Might it be sad? Might it be worried, or left-out?

00:01:44.564 --> 00:01:50.135
Every suspect is allowed. A feeling can be a "might be" while we look.

00:01:50.135 --> 00:01:56.634
Step four: pick the closest word, just for now. Our pretend feeling might be… worried. Worried fits the clues best.

00:01:56.634 --> 00:02:04.062
The word can change later. Detectives keep looking, and feelings can too.

00:02:04.062 --> 00:02:06.848
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:02:06.848 --> 00:02:10.562
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:02:10.562 --> 00:02:14.276
You're ready for what's next.
